---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const html = '<p>A cash balance plan is a bad fit for someone who wants a one-year tax trick. It is a reasonable fit for someone who can fund through a few ordinary years and will call when a year is not ordinary.</p>\n<h2>The moments that need a meeting</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Profit drops.</strong> Do not skip a deposit and hope. The actuary can discuss an amendment or a freeze. Quiet nonpayment collides with minimum funding.</li>\n<li><strong>You hire.</strong> Last year’s census is not this year’s test.</li>\n<li><strong>You sell the practice.</strong> The plan’s assets and liabilities have to be dealt with in the deal, not discovered at closing. Termination, or a spin, is a project.</li>\n<li><strong>You are done.</strong> Termination means a final valuation, filings, and usually a distribution or rollover to an IRA. It is not a form you download in an afternoon.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Annual administration — census, testing, notices, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/form-5500-corner">Form 5500</a> — is the quiet middle. Dates live on the <a href="/calendar">calendar</a>. If you are already a client, <a href="/support">support</a> is the right door. If you are deciding whether to start, read <a href="/not-a-fit">when not to</a> and then <a href="/contact">bring the facts</a>.</p>';
---
<Base title="The plan after the sale, the bad year, and the exit. | Savant Pensions">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">After adoption</p>
    <h1>After the cash balance plan exists.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Adopting is the start. Freezing, amending, and terminating are part of the design.</p>
    <div class="guide" set:html={html} />
  </section>
</Base>
